  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Nisar Hasan Chougule vs State Of Maharashtra on 7 October, 2023 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 902-Aba-2798-23.Doc Sayali Upasani In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2798 Of 2023 Nisar Hasan Chougule ...Applicant Vs. The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Mr. Shaikh Asif Ali i/b A. A. Siddhiquie and Associates, for Applicant. Mrs. Ashwini A. Takalkar, App for State. Mr. V. S. Waigankar, Psi, Roha Police Station, Present. Coram:- N. J. Jamadar, J. DATED:- 7th OCTOBER, 2023 PC:- 1) Heard the learned counsel for the applicant and the learned APP for the State.",
    "facts": "On 19th August, 2023 at about 5.05 am near Varse Stop, the co-accused - Dilip Palange, was found in possession of contraband articles - Gutka Pan Masala. The prosecution alleges that it transpired that the accused No. 1 had purchased the contraband articles from the applicant. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with C.R. No.136 of 2023 registered with Roha Police Station, for the offences punishable under Sections 328 r/w. 34 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 ('IPC' for short) and Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(d), 27(3)(e) and 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. According to the allegations in the FIR, co-accused - Dilip Palange, was found in possession of contraband articles being Gutakha Pan Masala and the present Applicant has been named by Nisar Hasan Chougule vs State Of Maharashtra on 28 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/127970361/ 1 co-accused persons. Admittedly, the Applicant is protected by order dated 07.10.2023 for last about 2 years. Learned APP on instructions of Head Constable of the concerned Police Station (who is present in the Court) submits that the Applicant has so far co-operated with the investigation and the charge-sheet is already filed and case is registered as R.C. No.15 of 2025, J.M.F.C. Roha, Raigad.",
